resources.string:
MD Reader (the “App”) is developed and operated by 刘什么 (“we”, “us”). We care about your privacy. Please read this Privacy Policy carefully before using the App to understand how information related to the App is handled and what rights you have.

The App is a local-first document reader. It has no servers of its own and does not upload your bookshelf, notes, or reading history to us.

1. What information we process

1.1 Information stored locally on your device
The following information is stored only on your device by default (app-private directory, local database, local preferences), and we cannot access it remotely:
1. Books and documents: copies or references of imported Markdown, text, PDF, HTML, and source files, plus GitHub project workspaces, used to display your bookshelf and read documents;
2. Reading data: reading progress, bookmarks, multi-color highlights, notes, reading time, and word-count statistics, used to restore your position, manage notes, and show statistics;
3. Profile data: the nickname, bio, and avatar you set in “Me”, shown only inside the App;
4. Preferences: theme, language, font, line spacing, page margins, page-turn mode, and per-format reading styles, used to remember your reading habits;
5. Cache: temporary files such as network images, PDF page images, and rendered diagrams, used to speed up loading and clearable in the App;
6. WebDAV settings: the server address, account, password, backup directory, and device name you enter, used to connect to the server you specify for backup.

1.2 Information produced only when you go online
Core reading features work offline. Network requests are made only when you actively use the following features:
1. Import a document by URL: requests the URL you enter and sends that URL plus standard request information (IP, User-Agent);
2. Load remote images in a document: requests the image URL and sends the same standard information;
3. Import a public GitHub repository: requests github.com and related GitHub domains and sends the repository address plus standard request information;
4. Open external links in a document: requests the URL you tap and sends the same standard information;
5. WebDAV backup and restore: requests the WebDAV server you configure and sends the backup package (bookshelf metadata, notes, optionally book content) and the account you configure;
6. Check for updates: requests raw.githubusercontent.com, cdn.jsdelivr.net, fastly.jsdelivr.net, and github.com and sends a version-comparison request plus standard request information.
These requests are triggered by you (WebDAV backup runs as an automatic task you enable). We do not send this content back to or retain it on our own servers. Third-party websites, image hosts, GitHub, and WebDAV providers may log access under their own privacy policies, which we do not control.

1.3 Information we do not collect
The App does not collect, read, or upload:
1. Device identifiers (IMEI, IMSI, MEID, OAID, Android ID, MAC address, serial number);
2. Contacts, call logs, or SMS;
3. Precise or approximate location;
4. Photos, camera, or microphone;
5. Installed app list;
6. Clipboard content (we only write when you tap “Copy”, and never read it);
7. ID documents, bank cards, or biometric information;
8. Advertising identifiers; we do not build user profiles or push personalized ads.
The App has no account system and does not require sign-in, so there is no account deletion process.

2. Device permissions and purposes
The permissions declared in system settings and their purposes are (all are normal permissions, none are sensitive):
1. INTERNET (network access): import documents by URL, load remote images, import GitHub repositories, open external links, WebDAV backup, and check for updates; used when you invoke the related feature;
2. ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE (view network state): check whether a network is available before a background backup task runs;
3. WAKE_LOCK (keep awake): keep the CPU awake during background backup tasks so they are not interrupted;
4. RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED (boot broadcast): restore the “daily automatic backup” plan you enabled after the device boots;
5. FOREGROUND_SERVICE (foreground service): run long-running tasks such as backup reliably in the background.
The App does not request storage permissions (READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE, WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE, MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE). Imported files are authorized one at a time through the system file picker, and exported notes are saved via the system “Save as” dialog; the App can access only the file you select.
You can view and disable these permissions at any time in “Settings → Apps → MD Reader → Permissions”. Disabling them disables the related features but does not affect local reading.

3. Third-party SDKs and open-source components
The App does not integrate any third-party SDK for advertising, analytics, push notifications, social sharing, payments, or crash reporting that collects personal information.
The App uses the following open-source components, which run locally and do not actively collect or upload personal information: AndroidX, Jetpack Compose, Hilt, Room, DataStore, WorkManager, OkHttp, JGit, Markwon, JLaTeXMath, Vico, Gson, and others. You can find the full dependency list and licenses on the App’s “About” page or in the open-source repository.
Rendering HTML documents, opening external links, and drawing diagrams use the system WebView; page content is provided by the corresponding website and is subject to its privacy policy.

4. Storage and protection
1. Location: local data is stored on your device and is deleted when you uninstall the App or clear its data.
2. Retention: you control it. You can delete books, bookmarks, and notes at any time or clear the cache in the App; uninstalling deletes all local data.
3. Security: the app-private directory is protected by the Android sandbox and cannot be read directly by other apps; network requests use HTTPS, and release builds block cleartext HTTP (except local debugging addresses).
4. WebDAV credentials: the account and password are stored in the app-private directory and used only to connect to the server you specify. Use a WebDAV service you trust and keep your account safe.
5. System backup: if you enable Android “cloud backup / device migration”, the system may back up the App database according to your settings. This is controlled by the operating system and can be turned off in system settings.
6. Cross-border transfer: we do not store your information outside your country. When you access GitHub, overseas image hosts, or other overseas services, requests are sent to those providers and handled under their local rules.

5. Sharing, transfer, and public disclosure
We do not sell your personal information or share or transfer your local reading data with third parties, except:
1. with your separate consent;
2. when you use URL import, remote images, GitHub import, WebDAV backup, or external links, necessary requests are sent to the provider you specify to complete that feature;
3. when required by laws and regulations, by competent authorities, or to protect your, others’, or the public’s lawful rights.

6. Your rights
To the extent permitted by law, you have the right to:
1. Access and correct: view and edit your nickname, bio, and avatar in “Me”; view reading data on the bookshelf and notes pages.
2. Delete: delete books, bookmarks, highlights, and notes, and clear the cache; files in WebDAV backups can be deleted on your own server.
3. Withdraw consent: disable permissions in system settings, stop using WebDAV and other online features, or uninstall the App.
4. Opt out of personalization: the App does not recommend content or push ads.
5. Complaints and questions: contact us using the details at the end of this Policy; we will reply within 15 business days.

7. Children’s privacy
The App is a document reader with general content suitable for ages 3 and up. If you are a child under 14, please use the App with your guardian’s consent and guidance. If a guardian finds that a minor has provided personal information to us, contact us using the details below and we will handle it promptly.

8. Changes to this Policy
We may update this Policy from time to time. When we do, we will publish the new version in the App and update the “Last updated” date. If a change significantly affects your rights, we will notify you more prominently, such as with a dialog, and it will take effect after you confirm.

9. Contact us
Operator: 刘什么
Email: 2461543643@qq.com
Website: https://liushenme.space
Feedback: https://github.com/liushenme1999/MarkdownReader/issues
If you have any questions, comments, or complaints about this Policy or our handling of personal information, please contact us using the details above.

ICP filing: 京ICP备2024097076号-3A
